        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{13}{100}$",
          "worked": "The intersection of “No accidents” and “Younger than 28” contains 650 drivers.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{no accidents and younger than 28})&=\\frac{650}{5000}\\\\P(\\text{no accidents and younger than 28})&=\\frac{13}{100}\\end{align*}$$",
